{
  "wireMagic": "pb3",
  "pens": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wsWinStyles": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wpWinPositions": [ {
  
  } ],
  "events": [ {
    "tStartMs": 160,
    "dDurationMs": 3280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "One single scientist created\nthree inventions"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3440,
    "dDurationMs": 3840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that accidentally caused the deaths\nof millions of people,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 7840,
    "dDurationMs": 1440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "including himself."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 10000,
    "dDurationMs": 3760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Not only that, they decreased the \naverage intelligence of people "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 13760,
    "dDurationMs": 1280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "all around the world,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 15040,
    "dDurationMs": 1440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "increased crime rates,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 16480,
    "dDurationMs": 3600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and caused two completely \nseparate environmental disasters"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 20080,
    "dDurationMs": 2400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that we are still dealing with today."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 24080,
    "dDurationMs": 2160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Part of this video is\nsponsored by Wren."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 26240,
    "dDurationMs": 3600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "More about them at the end of the show."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 30400,
    "dDurationMs": 3360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In 1944, as a young chemist\nwho had just finished his"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 33760,
    "dDurationMs": 4320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Master's, Clair Patterson went\nto work on the Manhattan Project,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 38080,
    "dDurationMs": 2880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "building the first\nnuclear weapons."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 40960,
    "dDurationMs": 5600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "His job was to concentrate uranium-235,\nthe fissile fuel for bombs"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 46560,
    "dDurationMs": 2960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "from the much more common\nuranium-238."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 49520,
    "dDurationMs": 5520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And this required huge machines, mass\nspectrometers, which separated"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 55040,
    "dDurationMs": 3440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the two types of uranium by\ntheir slight difference in mass."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 64560,
    "dDurationMs": 3200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "After the war, Patterson went\nback to grad school to get his"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 67760,
    "dDurationMs": 3280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "PhD, he picked a research\nproject that would take"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 71040,
    "dDurationMs": 2800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "advantage of his experience\nwith mass spectrometers:"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 74480,
    "dDurationMs": 2080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "measuring the age of the\nEarth."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 78400,
    "dDurationMs": 3520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Radioactive rocks are\neffectively clocks."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 81920,
    "dDurationMs": 4960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Uranium-238, for example, decays into\nthorium and then protactinium,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 86880,
    "dDurationMs": 4560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and then 12 More decays until\nit ends up as lead-206, which is stable."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 92080,
    "dDurationMs": 3040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The rate of this\ndecay is consistent and can be"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 95120,
    "dDurationMs": 4160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "measured. It takes four and a\nhalf billion years for half of"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 99280,
    "dDurationMs": 3840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "a sample of U-238. to decay\ninto lead-206"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 103840,
    "dDurationMs": 4480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Patterson's PhD project was to determine the\nage of the Earth by measuring"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 108320,
    "dDurationMs": 3600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the ratio of uranium to lead\nin primordial rocks,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 112560,
    "dDurationMs": 4320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but to calibrate his instrument, first\nhe used zircon crystals whose"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 116880,
    "dDurationMs": 1040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "ages were known."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 118640,
    "dDurationMs": 2160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Zircon is ideal for this purpose,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 120800,
    "dDurationMs": 3040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "because when it forms it\ncontains trace amounts of"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 123840,
    "dDurationMs": 2480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "uranium but absolutely no\nlead."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 126880,
    "dDurationMs": 4880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So any lead that you later find inside a zircon,\nyou know must be the product"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 131760,
    "dDurationMs": 1200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of a uranium decay."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 134000,
    "dDurationMs": 3040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Patterson was tasked with \nmeasuring the lead content,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 137040,
    "dDurationMs": 2800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and another student, George \nTilton, measured uranium"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 141280,
    "dDurationMs": 3600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Tilton 's uranium measurements\nwere fine. They matched predictions."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 145520,
    "dDurationMs": 2400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But Patterson's\nlead measurements were all"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 147920,
    "dDurationMs": 3040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "over the place. And they were\nmany many times higher than"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 150960,
    "dDurationMs": 1040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "they expected."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 152000,
    "dDurationMs": 2240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "We'd take George's uranium and my lead..."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 154800,
    "dDurationMs": 1040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Not right Patterson!"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 157200,
    "dDurationMs": 1840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "There was lead there that\ndidn't belong there."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 160480,
    "dDurationMs": 2640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So where was all this extra\nlead coming from?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 163920,
    "dDurationMs": 4560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "That mystery would take over the rest of\nClair Patterson's life"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 168480,
    "dDurationMs": 2960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and bring him to the literal ends\nof the earth."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 174400,
    "dDurationMs": 3840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In 1908, a woman was driving\nacross the Belle Isle bridge"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 178240,
    "dDurationMs": 2240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "in Detroit. When her car\nstalled."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 181120,
    "dDurationMs": 2240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "A passing motorist stopped to help."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 183360,
    "dDurationMs": 3200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In those days\ncars needed to be hand cranked to start."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 187280,
    "dDurationMs": 2800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "He knelt down and\nturned the crank,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 190080,
    "dDurationMs": 3440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and the engine roared to life. A\nlittle too suddenly."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 194080,
    "dDurationMs": 3440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The man couldn't get out of the way.\nThe crank handle hit him in"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 197520,
    "dDurationMs": 1680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the face and broke his jaw."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 200480,
    "dDurationMs": 2240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "He died as a result of his\ninjuries."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 203360,
    "dDurationMs": 4960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "His name was Byron Carter, and he was the founder\nof his own car company."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 208320,
    "dDurationMs": 2960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So he was well connected in the\nDetroit Auto scene."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 211280,
    "dDurationMs": 4000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "He counted among his close friends, the\nfounder of Cadillac, Henry Leland."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 216000,
    "dDurationMs": 2480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Leland was so\ndistraught over his friend's"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 218480,
    "dDurationMs": 4480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "death that he resolved to\neliminate hand cranks from his vehicles."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 224000,
    "dDurationMs": 2827,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Leland hired Charles\nKettering to create a self-"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 226827,
    "dDurationMs": 4053,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "starting car. And by 1911, he\nhad a working prototype."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 231760,
    "dDurationMs": 4400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Hand cranking was difficult and\ndangerous, and best left to men,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 237200,
    "dDurationMs": 3040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but a car that started itself"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 240240,
    "dDurationMs": 1440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "changed everything."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 242400,
    "dDurationMs": 1680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The world's first crankless car"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 244080,
    "dDurationMs": 3120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "was the Cadillac Model 30. It\nwas much more powerful than"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 247200,
    "dDurationMs": 4000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "cars before it. It had a top\nspeed of 45 miles per hour and"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 251200,
    "dDurationMs": 4560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "40 horsepower, double the Ford\nModel T. The Model 30 was a"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 255760,
    "dDurationMs": 3440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "huge success for Cadillac,\ndoubling the company's annual"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 259200,
    "dDurationMs": 4720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "sales, but it had a problem.\nIt was deafeningly loud."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 265360,
    "dDurationMs": 4320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In internal combustion engines\na piston compresses the fuel-air mixture,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 269680,
    "dDurationMs": 3120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "which is then\nignited by a spark from the spark plug."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 272800,
    "dDurationMs": 3200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The expanding hot\ngases push the piston back down."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 276640,
    "dDurationMs": 2480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The problem with the\nModel 30 engine was it"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 279120,
    "dDurationMs": 2960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "compressed the fuel-air\nmixture more than previous"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 282080,
    "dDurationMs": 3040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "models so much in fact, that\noften the fuel would"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 285120,
    "dDurationMs": 3840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "spontaneously combust before\nthe spark from the spark plug."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 288960,
    "dDurationMs": 2880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So rather than orderly,\nperfectly timed explosions,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 291840,
    "dDurationMs": 3440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "you'd get multiple haphazard\ncombustions leading to"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 295280,
    "dDurationMs": 2880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "turbulent pressure waves\ninside the cylinder. The"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 298160,
    "dDurationMs": 1760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "resulting sound led the\nproblem"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 299920,
    "dDurationMs": 2160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "To become known as engine\nknocking."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 303520,
    "dDurationMs": 3280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Knocking wasn't just hard on\nthe ears, it hurt the engine's"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 306800,
    "dDurationMs": 3200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "performance, it reduced power\noutput and lowered fuel"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 310000,
    "dDurationMs": 3520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "efficiency. The vibrations\nalso damaged the piston and"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 313520,
    "dDurationMs": 2400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "walls of the cylinder\nshortening the life of the"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 315920,
    "dDurationMs": 320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "engine."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 317440,
    "dDurationMs": 3200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The good news was that engine\nknocking could be corrected by"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 320640,
    "dDurationMs": 3920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "changing the fuel. Different\nfuels can withstand different"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 324560,
    "dDurationMs": 3760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "levels of compression before\ndetonating n-heptane for"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 328320,
    "dDurationMs": 3360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "example, will spontaneously\ncombust under only a little"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 331680,
    "dDurationMs": 3600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "compression. Iso-octane, on\nthe other hand can withstand a"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 335280,
    "dDurationMs": 4240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "much higher compression ratio\nbefore it auto ignites. So"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 339520,
    "dDurationMs": 3760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "it's much less likely to cause\nknocking. To quantify how much"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 343280,
    "dDurationMs": 2560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "compression a fuel can\nwithstand scientists came up"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 345840,
    "dDurationMs": 3280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "with the octane rating system,\nthey arbitrarily set"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 349120,
    "dDurationMs": 3920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "iso-octane to have a rating of\n100 and n-heptane a rating of"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 353040,
    "dDurationMs": 3200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "zero. Now real fuels aren't\nmade up of only these two"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 356240,
    "dDurationMs": 2240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "ingredients. They're a mix of\nlots of different"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 358480,
    "dDurationMs": 3280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "hydrocarbons. But the octane\nrating tells you what mixture"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 361760,
    "dDurationMs": 3600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of octane and heptane gives\nequivalent performance. For"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 365360,
    "dDurationMs": 3600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "example, 98 octane fuel can\nwithstand the same compression"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 368960,
    "dDurationMs": 4400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "as a mixture of 98% octane and\n2% heptane. Now, I'm going to"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 373360,
    "dDurationMs": 3760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "take a little bit of 98 octane\nfuel and put it in this"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 377920,
    "dDurationMs": 2560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "piston. And when I compress\nit,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 382560,
    "dDurationMs": 3120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "nothing happens which is\nexactly what you'd expect."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 385680,
    "dDurationMs": 3600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This fuel can withstand a lot\nof compression. Diesel has an"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 389280,
    "dDurationMs": 3120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "octane rating of 20. So it\nacts like a mixture of 20%"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 392400,
    "dDurationMs": 3520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "iso-octane and 80% n-heptane.\nIf I put a little bit of"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 395920,
    "dDurationMs": 3200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "diesel in there, let's see\nwhat happens with the same"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 399120,
    "dDurationMs": 960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "compression ratio."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 406560,
    "dDurationMs": 2880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "There you go. You get a little\nexplosion in there. That's"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 409440,
    "dDurationMs": 2400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "because this is a low octane\nfuel. I mean, that's what"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 411840,
    "dDurationMs": 2800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "diesel is meant to do. You\ncompress it and it ignites."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 414640,
    "dDurationMs": 3360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But you don't want this sort\nof fuel in an engine with"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 418000,
    "dDurationMs": 4240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "spark plugs. The reason fancy\ncars demand high octane fuel"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 422240,
    "dDurationMs": 2480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "is to prevent knocking in\ntheir high-compression"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 424720,
    "dDurationMs": 1280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "high-performance engines."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 428000,
    "dDurationMs": 2640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Kettering wanted to find an\nadditive which would increase"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 430640,
    "dDurationMs": 3440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the octane rating of ordinary\nfuel and eliminate knocking in"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 434080,
    "dDurationMs": 3440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "high-compression engines. So\nhe hired a 27-year-old"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 437520,
    "dDurationMs": 4320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "engineer Thomas Midgley Jr.\nMidgley experimented with all"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 441840,
    "dDurationMs": 4320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "sorts of compounds from melted\nbutter and camphor, to ethyl"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 446160,
    "dDurationMs": 3600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "acetate and aluminum chloride.\nHe later wrote, most of them"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 449760,
    "dDurationMs": 2480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "had no more effect than\nspitting in the Great Lakes."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 453680,
    "dDurationMs": 3120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Ethanol was an interesting\nexception, it did stop the"
    } ]
  }, {
